# Task Template
#CHLOEAI:1
TYPE="task"

# ============================================================
# HOW TO USE THIS TEMPLATE
# ============================================================
#
# Copy this template when creating a new task.
# Fill in each section. Delete sections that don't apply.
# Save as: TASK_<short-name>.chloeai
#
# Tasks live alongside the code they affect or in a tasks/ folder.
# The AI reads these to understand what work needs doing.
# Wy creates them. The AI executes and logs results.

# ============================================================
# TASK
# ============================================================

TASK_ID=""
TITLE=""
STATUS=""          # open | in-progress | blocked | done | cancelled
PRIORITY=""        # critical | high | normal | low
CREATED=""         # ISO 8601 timestamp
VERSION_TARGET=""  # Which version should this land in?

# ============================================================
# DESCRIPTION
# ============================================================
#
# What needs to happen? Be specific.
# Include the "why" -- what problem does this solve?
# Include acceptance criteria -- how do we know it's done?
#
# WHAT:
#
#
# WHY:
#
#
# DONE WHEN:
#   - [ ]
#   - [ ]
#   - [ ]

# ============================================================
# CONTEXT
# ============================================================
#
# What does the AI need to know before starting?
# Link to relevant files, previous experiments, known constraints.
#
# RELEVANT FILES:
#   -
#
# PRIOR ATTEMPTS:
#   - (reference experiment IDs from PROJECT_STATE.chloeai if any)
#
# CONSTRAINTS:
#   - (things that must NOT change, compatibility requirements, etc.)

# ============================================================
# APPROACH (AI fills this in)
# ============================================================
#
# Before executing, the AI documents the planned approach here.
# Wy reviews and approves before execution begins.
#
# PLAN:
#
#
# ASSUMPTIONS:
#   -
#
# RISKS:
#   -
#
# APPROVED: [ ] yes / [ ] no (Wy checks this)

# ============================================================
# EXECUTION LOG (AI fills this in)
# ============================================================
#
# Track what was actually done, step by step.
# Use the experiment format from the personality script.
#
# CHANGES:
#   @timestamp|
#   change=""|
#   expect=""|
#   observe=""|
#   location=""|
#   status=

# ============================================================
# TESTING
# ============================================================
#
# What needs to be tested? How?
# The human fills in results in WORKSHEET.heywy after testing.
#
# TEST PLAN:
#   - [ ]
#   - [ ]
#
# WORKSHEET REFERENCE:
#   (AI adds pointer to WORKSHEET.heywy test report section)

# ============================================================
# RESULT
# ============================================================
#
# Final outcome. Filled in when task is done or cancelled.
#
# OUTCOME=""       # completed | partial | failed | cancelled
# VERSION=""       # What version was this shipped in?
# NOTES=""         # Anything the next session should know

# END OF TASK TEMPLATE
